# Copy to `.env` and fill in. Never commit `.env`.
#
# In `.env`, not `.env.local`: the Prisma CLI does not read `.env.local`, so splitting
# these gives you a working app and a failing `prisma migrate`.

# Two connection strings, with different owners.
#
# DATABASE_URL — TRANSACTION pooler, port 6543. The app, because a serverless function
# opens a connection per invocation and would exhaust a direct one.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?pgbouncer=true"

# DIRECT_URL — SESSION pooler, port 5432. Migrations, because `prisma migrate` cannot
# run over transaction-mode pooling.
#
# `?schema=paste` belongs on this URL and NOT on DATABASE_URL. It decides which schema
# holds `_prisma_migrations`, which matters because the Supabase project is shared: a
# ledger in `public` is a ledger every app in the project writes to, and each app then
# reads the others' migrations as applied-but-missing-from-disk. The runtime needs no
# equivalent — the generated client qualifies every table as "paste"."…".
DIRECT_URL="postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres?schema=paste"

# DATABASE_POOL_MAX — connections per process, default 3. Set it to 6 in deployment.
# Each serverless invocation is its own process with its own pool, so the ceiling that
# matters is (instances × max), not max. Left low locally, where nothing is concurrent.
# DATABASE_POOL_MAX=6

# Prefer `pooler.supabase.com` over `db.<project-ref>.supabase.co`, which is IPv6-only
# without the paid IPv4 add-on. If port 6543 is blocked on your network, point both at
# :5432, drop `?pgbouncer=true`, and treat the transaction pooler as untested until
# deploy day. `28P01` is a wrong password; `ETIMEDOUT` is a blocked port.

# The second origin serving /raw and /dl, so the cookie isolation ARCHITECTURE §6.5
# depends on is exercised locally. Run `pnpm dev:raw` alongside `pnpm dev`. Unset means
# both are served from the app origin — a knowing compromise.
NEXT_PUBLIC_RAW_ORIGIN="http://127.0.0.1:3026"

# PASTE_ORIGIN — this app's own origin, e.g. https://paste.example.com
#
# Pins the destination of the proxy's internal self-fetch, which is how /p/:id gets a real
# 410 (src/proxy.ts explains why the page cannot set one). Unset, the destination falls
# back to the origin Next resolved from the Host header; Next normalises that and a forged
# Host was measured not to redirect it, but relying on a framework detail for "this server
# will not fetch an attacker's origin and serve the result as its own" is not a trade worth
# making in production. SET THIS IN DEPLOYMENT.
# PASTE_ORIGIN="https://<your-domain>"

# CRON_SECRET — the shared secret for POST /api/renders (the render backfill) and, from
# M9, the expiry and purge sweeps. The endpoint returns 503 rather than running when this
# is unset: fail closed, because an unauthenticated endpoint that invokes a highlighter is
# a way to make the server do unbounded WASM work on demand.
# CRON_SECRET="<a long random string>"

# Object storage, for bodies over 512 KB. Server-only, never NEXT_PUBLIC_: the browser
# never talks to Supabase, and the bucket is PRIVATE so bodies are served through /raw and
# /dl where expiry and redaction still apply. Create the bucket once in the dashboard:
# Storage -> New bucket, name "paste-bodies", Public OFF.
#
# Unset, a create over 512 KB fails loudly rather than silently storing inline, and the
# storage round-trip tests skip.
SUPABASE_URL="https://<project-ref>.supabase.co"
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY="<service-role-key — bypasses RLS, never commit>"

# SWEEP_BUDGET_MS — wall clock for one sweeper invocation. Default 240000, capped at
# 290000 so the function always returns its summary rather than being killed mid-run.
# SWEEP_BUDGET_MS=240000
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY / CLERK_SECRET_KEY — auth (M10).

# Marks the proxy's own self-fetch, so a client cannot forge it.
#
# Optional. Unset, it falls back to a per-process random value — correct for one server and
# for the test suite. SET IT in any deployment running more than one instance: a self-fetch
# landing on a neighbour would otherwise look like an external request. Any long random
# string; it never leaves the server.
PASTE_INTERNAL_TOKEN=
